    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db50aa15_d6dcc26a",
        "filename": "common/audio_codec.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-12T08:28:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not a big fan of these \"register\" functions in the EC (yes, that\u0027s how the kernel is structure, but they don\u0027t have such space constraints):\n 1. They take up code space for little value (and prevent LTO inlining)\n 2. They break stack analyzer (or we need to add some annotations)\n\nCan you just call audio_codec_translate_addr_ec_to_ap(), and have the relevant audio codec driver define that function? This assumes there is a single audio codec per board, of course.",
      "revId": "20cc71f25c6faedfac9d1f175325cadbd227c24f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0aa70de7_6f39dd7a",
        "filename": "common/audio_codec.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1275795
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-19T02:06:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Did you mean: let it have only one audio_codec_translate_addr_ec_to_ap() symbol when linking?\n\u003d\u003e if so, the method sounds fragile to me\n\nI am wondering if it is possible to add some constrains to keep these register_* functions:\n1. arrange register_* functions in .init section\n2. only .init section can use register_* functions\n3. after initialization, the .init section will be freed (and available)\n\nIn my original plan, I would only wish only HOOK_INIT calls these register_* functions but not in any runtime (see https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/1424041/30/board/kukui_scp/audio_codec_wov.c#53).\n\nNote: the .init section mechanism is similar to kernel",
      "parentUuid": "db50aa15_d6dcc26a",
      "revId": "20cc71f25c6faedfac9d1f175325cadbd227c24f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "093849f6_2a8758ed",
        "filename": "common/audio_codec.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-22T00:56:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Did you mean: let it have only one audio_codec_translate_addr_ec_to_ap() symbol when linking?\n\u003e \u003d\u003e if so, the method sounds fragile to me\n\nWell, that\u0027s how EC code generally works.\n\n\u003e 3. after initialization, the .init section will be freed (and available)\n\nThere is no concept of \"freeing memory\" in EC. No malloc, no free.\n\nYes, kernel does this too, but kernel doesn\u0027t care about code size (or doesn\u0027t care as much), we do.",
      "parentUuid": "0aa70de7_6f39dd7a",
      "revId": "20cc71f25c6faedfac9d1f175325cadbd227c24f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
